{%- doc -%}
  Prints two facts about the collection that holds a model's colourways, as
  `count~^~first_product_id`.

  Staging keeps one collection per model, handle-matched to the group tag
  (`collection::CYRUS` → `cyrus`), which makes it the only page-independent
  source of truth on the grouped PLP: `count` is the real colourway total that
  a 50-product page can't see, and `first_product_id` names one colourway as
  the model's representative so the same card can't appear on two pages.

  Only an exact handle or title match counts — a curated collection the product
  happens to sit in must never be mistaken for the model. Both fields come back
  blank when there's no match, and the caller falls back to page-scoped
  grouping.

  `first_product_id` costs a product fetch, so ask for it only when needed.

  @param {object} product - a colourway of the model
  @param {string} group_name - model name from the group tag
  @param {boolean} [want_first] - also print the representative's id

  @example
  {%- capture facts -%}
    {%- render 'spy-model-collection-facts', product: product, group_name: name -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign facts = facts | strip | split: '~^~' -%}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign total = ''
  assign first_id = ''

  if group_name != blank
    assign group_key = group_name | handleize
    assign group_title = group_name | downcase | strip

    for col in product.collections
      assign col_title = col.title | downcase | strip
      if col.handle == group_key or col_title == group_title
        assign total = col.all_products_count
        if want_first
          assign first_id = col.products.first.id
        endif
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  echo total
  echo '~^~'
  echo first_id
-%}
